[
  {
    "pkheadingid": 821,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Definition",
    "headingPosition": 1,
    "headingid": 764,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 127699,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 248,
        "headingId": 764,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Sinusoidal haemangioma is a histologically distinctive benign vascular lesion consisting of thin-walled vascular channels with scant smooth muscle in a sinusoidal or sieve-like pattern, and with features resembling those of anastomosing haemangioma (a lesion seen mainly in the kidney).</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-25T11:55:34"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 822,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-O coding",
    "headingPosition": 2,
    "headingid": 765,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 127700,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 248,
        "headingId": 765,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>9120/0 Sinusoidal haemangioma</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-25T11:55:34"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 823,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-11 coding",
    "headingPosition": 3,
    "headingid": 766,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 127701,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 248,
        "headingId": 766,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>2F2Y &amp; XH88L5 Other specified benign cutaneous neoplasms &amp; Sinusoidal haemangioma</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-25T11:55:34"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 824,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Related terminology",
    "headingPosition": 4,
    "headingid": 767,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 127702,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 248,
        "headingId": 767,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>Acceptable:</em> sinusoidal venous malformation.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-25T11:55:34"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 825,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Subtype(s)",
    "headingPosition": 5,
    "headingid": 768,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 127703,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 248,
        "headingId": 768,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>None</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-25T11:55:34"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 826,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Localization",
    "headingPosition": 6,
    "headingid": 769,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 127704,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 248,
        "headingId": 769,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>The most common location is the trunk. Subcutaneous tissue of the breast and extremities can be affected.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-25T11:55:34"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 827,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Clinical features",
    "headingPosition": 7,
    "headingid": 770,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 127705,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 248,
        "headingId": 770,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>The lesion is a small, asymptomatic, well-demarcated acquired dermal or subcutaneous bluish nodule.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-25T11:55:34"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 828,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Epidemiology",
    "headingPosition": 8,
    "headingid": 771,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 127706,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 248,
        "headingId": 771,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>These relatively rare lesions occur primarily in middle-aged women. In men, they frequently develop in the setting of gynaecomastia.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-25T11:55:34"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 829,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Etiology",
    "headingPosition": 9,
    "headingid": 772,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 127707,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 248,
        "headingId": 772,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>The etiology is unknown, but many consider this to be a venous malformation with delayed presentation.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-25T11:55:34"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 830,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Pathogenesis",
    "headingPosition": 10,
    "headingid": 773,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 127708,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 248,
        "headingId": 773,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Unknown</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-25T11:55:34"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 837,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Macroscopic appearance",
    "headingPosition": 11,
    "headingid": 780,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 127709,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 248,
        "headingId": 780,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>See <em>Clinical features</em>, above.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-25T11:55:34"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 831,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Histopathology",
    "headingPosition": 12,
    "headingid": 774,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 127710,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 248,
        "headingId": 774,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>The lesions are lobular and relatively well circumscribed. They are composed of irregular, dilated, congested, thin-walled vascular channels with scant smooth muscle in a sinusoidal or sieve-like pattern, with little intervening stroma {1746680; 26945338; 19606014}. The endothelial cells are uniform and mitotically quiescent. Thrombosis and dystrophic calcification are often present. A similar sinusoidal vascular pattern is commonly seen focally in venous malformations.</p>\r\n<h6>Differential diagnosis</h6>\r\n<p>In the breast, the differential diagnosis includes well-differentiated angiosarcoma. However, angiosarcoma shows multilayering of endothelial cells, cytological atypia, and mitotic activity.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-25T11:55:34"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 832,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Cytology",
    "headingPosition": 13,
    "headingid": 775,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 127711,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 248,
        "headingId": 775,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-25T11:55:34"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 833,
